. *****************************************************************************
> ***
. ****************** Do-File H2: ManyDaughters Project ******************
. *****************************************************************************
> ***
. 
. * Changes from PAP
. * The variable "hgnrpers" denoting number of persons living in a household fr
> om the dataset "pgen" that was present in the documentation was unfortunately
>  not featured in the datasets made available to us, therefore we could not ca
> lculate the Nr of Adults control variable and consequently we dropped it from
>  the analyses. 
. * Recoded negative values for all control variables as missing values 
. * When constructing HavingDaughter variable per Wave, we have counted with ki
> ds-related variables from the year prior (so HavingDaughters for 2005 runs ou
> r pre-defined construction formula with kids from before 2005)
. * We have dropped the following individual-difference control variables from 
> the final model because they were static: Education, Immigration Status, Sex
. * EastWest: will we code East as 0 and West as 1
. 
. 
. * Authors: [REDACTED] & [REDACTED]
. 
. * ============================
. * Setup *
. * ============================
. 
. *clear all
. version 19.5

. set maxvar 10000


. 
. * Install PACKAGES
. * ssc install reghdfe, replace
. * ssc install ftools, replace
. /*
> * CONFIGURE FILE PATHS * (Please do not change)
> * the following code automatically sets paths based on where you saved the di
> stributed file-package on your system *
> if strpos("`c(pwd)'", "code") {
>     global ROOT "`c(pwd)'/.."
> }
> else {
>     global ROOT "`c(pwd)'"
> }
> global IN "$ROOT/data/raw" // folder, in which the original datasets are stor
> ed
> global DATA "$ROOT/data/derived" // folder for datasets
> global OUT "$ROOT/out" // folder for output (results, tables)
> */
. 
. * ============================
. * Load and Merge Data *
. * ============================
. 
. use "$IN/pl.dta", clear //
(SOEP-Core, v37 (EU Edition), doi:10.5684/soep.core.v37eu)

. merge 1:1 pid syear using "$IN/ppathl.dta", keep(master match) nogen

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                            35,228  
    -----------------------------------------

. merge 1:1 pid syear using "$IN/pgen.dta", keep(match) nogen keepusing(pgfamst
> d pgpartz pgbilzeit pgnation)
(variable syear was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                            35,228  
    -----------------------------------------

. merge m:1 pid using "$IN/biobirth.dta", keep(match) nogen keepusing(kidsex01-
> kidsex19 sumkids kidgeb01-kidgeb19)
(variable pid was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(label sex already defined)
(label sex_EN already defined)
(label pid_EN already defined)
(label cid_EN already defined)
(label cid already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                            35,228  
    -----------------------------------------

. 
. * ============================
. * Data Preparation *
. * ============================
. 
. * Filter waves of interest
. keep if inlist(syear, 2005, 2009, 2014, 2019)
(28,692 observations deleted)

. 
. * Exclude respondents <18
. gen AgeP = syear - gebjahr

. keep if AgeP > 18
(491 observations deleted)

. 
. * Create Wave variable
. gen Wave = syear

. 
. * Recode political scale: LeftRight = 10 – plh0004, 0–10
. gen LeftRight = .
(6,045 missing values generated)

. replace LeftRight = 10 - plh0004 if inrange(plh0004,0,10)
(4,476 real changes made)

. 
. * Replace all negative values with missing in kidgeb01 to kidgeb19
. foreach v of varlist kidgeb01-kidgeb19 {
  2.     replace `v' = . if `v' < 0
  3. }
